    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Oden builds flavour through slow simmering. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Daikon",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "daikon"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " radish and potato take on the gentle flavour of the dashi broth over the course of an hour. "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Konnyaku",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "konnyaku"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " adds a satisfying chew that contrasts with the soft tofu and eggs. Serves 4."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Blanch the daikon in plain water first. This removes bitterness and gives it a cleaner flavour after long simmering."
          }
        ]
      },
